## CI policy (private repo — GitHub Free pool first, then Ubicloud)

CI minutes are one budget shared by every private repo. Never add a paid GitHub plan.

- **Local first.** Run the CI-equivalent commands before pushing. CI is a milestone check, not a debugger.
- **Draft until ready.** Open PRs as drafts; WIP commits carry `[skip ci]`; `gh pr ready` triggers the one CI run.
- **One run per ref.** No dispatch/empty-commit loops. After red: `gh run view <id> --log-failed`, fix locally, push once. Stop and report after three red runs. Infra flake: `gh run rerun <id> --failed` (all jobs after a "job was not started" refusal).
- **Runners.** Linux jobs never pin `ubuntu-*`: use a `runner` router job and `runs-on: ${{ needs.runner.outputs.label || 'ubicloud-standard-2' }}` (`-4` for heavy builds), or `runs-on: ubicloud-standard-2` directly when a whole run bills < 3 min. macOS/Windows stay GitHub-hosted (10x/2x) and only for releases. Public repos stay on GitHub-hosted.
- **Hygiene.** `pull_request` CI only (never push + PR on one branch); `push` only for deploy branches; `paths-ignore` docs; PR concurrency cancels, deploy concurrency does not; `timeout-minutes` on every job; no summary/gate jobs; never re-test in deploy what the PR passed; lowest useful cron.
- **Pool check** before releases: `python3 ~/.cursor/plugins/local/magik-repo/skills/ci-runners/scripts/ci_usage.py`. Full policy: rule/skill `ci-runners` in the magik-repo plugin.
